            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0106" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.203/201: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-23T16:00:00-04:00">December 23,
                            1942—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1653. The viewpoint expressed in the last sentence of section 2 of your no. 2177
                    of December 12, 6 p.m., has been discussed informally with the War Department,
                    which states that it appreciates the necessity for exemplary conduct on the part
                    of its personnel and that <pb facs="0107" n="95" xml:id="pg95"/> American troops
                    in Egypt are under standing instructions with respect thereto.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
